#!/bin/bash

# omarchy:summary=Explain how to change the Plymouth boot splash on NixOS.

# Upstream rebuilds the initramfs so a changed Plymouth theme takes effect.
# Here Plymouth is entirely a NixOS option (boot.plymouth, set from
# omarchy.seamless_boot.plymouth_theme) and there is no user config file at all.
# The initramfs is regenerated by nixos-rebuild, so there is nothing this can
# usefully do on its own.

set -euo pipefail

cat <<'MESSAGE'
Plymouth is configured by your flake, not by a file you edit here.

  There is no user Plymouth config on NixOS. The theme comes from
  omarchy.seamless_boot.plymouth_theme, and the initramfs that carries
  it is regenerated by nixos-rebuild.

To change the boot splash, set the theme and rebuild:

  omarchy.seamless_boot.plymouth_theme = "omarchy";
  sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake <your-flake>

Or from the menu, which writes that option for you:

  omarchy-opt-set omarchy.seamless_boot.plymouth_theme '"omarchy"'
MESSAGE
